{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-96974-r4530180","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Green Turtle Soup","sourcePageId":96974,"sourceRevision":"4530180","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-08-14T01:49:28Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Green%20Turtle%20Soup&oldid=4530180","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:54:35.000Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for soup","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using cayenne","Category:Recipes using crackers","Category:Recipes using egg yolk","Category:Recipes using lemon juice","Category:Recipes using sugar","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Turtle recipes","Category:United States recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"56ad59e0bf15f776d1fc07f94a3152bee6d61402538d71c7038fa671b4193e54","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Soup recipes\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\n'''Turtle soup''' is a [[cookbook:soup|soup]] made from the flesh of the turtle, often the green turtle or, especially in the [[cookbook:Cuisine of the United States|United States]], the snapping turtle, in which case it is commonly referred to as ''snapper soup'' (not to be confused with ''red snapper soup'', which is made from the fish called a red snapper).\n\nThis recipe is adapted from{{Gutenberg|13923}}\n==Ingredients==\n\n=== Forcemeat (optional) ===\n\n* 6 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] finely-chopped [[Cookbook:Turtle|turtle]] meat\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Hard Boiled Eggs|hard-boiled egg]] yolks\n* 1 tablespoon [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]]\n* [[Cookbook:Oyster|Oyster]] juice/liquor (optional)\n* Ground [[Cookbook:Cayenne Pepper|cayenne pepper]]\n* Ground [[Cookbook:Mace|mace]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Pinch|pinch]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Egg|eggs]]\n* [[Cookbook:Cracker|Cracker]] crumbs\n\n=== Soup ===\n* 1 whole turtle, cleaned\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Onion|onions]]\n* 1 bunch of sweet herbs\n* Brown flour\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Lemon|lemon]], juiced\n* 1 glass of Madeira [[Cookbook:Wine|wine]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n=== Forcemeat (optional) ===\n\n# Rub the minced turtle, yolks, butter, oyster liquor, cayenne, mace, sugar, and salt together to make a paste.\n# Mix in one of the eggs.\n# Shape the mixture into small balls. Dip in egg, then cracker crumbs.\n# Pan-fry in butter.\n\n=== Soup ===\n#After removing the entrails, cut up the coarser parts of the turtle meat and bones. Separate out the finer meat.\n#Place the coarse turtle in a pot with the onions, herbs, pepper, and salt. Cover with 4 [[Cookbook:Quart|quarts]] (4 [[Cookbook:Liter|liters]]) water, and simmer for 4 hours. Strain the broth, and discard the solids.\n#Simmer the finer turtle meat and the green fat for 1 hour in 2 quarts of water.\n#If there are eggs in the turtle, simmer them for 4 hours in water.\n#Reheat the broth in a pot, and add the fine turtle meat. Thicken with brown flour, and simmer gently for 1 hour.\n#Add the simmered eggs and/or forcemeat, lemon juice, and wine.\n#Serve hot.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* Green turtle can be purchased preserved in air-tight cans.\n* Some cooks add the finer meat before straining, boiling all together five hours; then strain, thicken and put in the green fat, cut into lumps an inch long. This makes a handsomer soup than if the meat is left in.\n\n==External links==\n*[http://www.bookbindersfoods.com/Prod_SoupsBisques.html Manufacturer of snapper soup]\n*[http://www.recipesource.com/soups/soups/19/rec1913.html Recipe for snapper soup]\n\n[[Category:Recipes for soup|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:United States recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Turtle recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg yolk]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon juice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cayenne]]\n[[Category:Recipes using crackers]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Green Turtle Soup","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"6 tablespoons finely-chopped turtle meat","sourceText":"6 tablespoons finely-chopped turtle meat","amountText":"6 tablespoons finely-chopped turtle meat","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 hard-boiled egg yolks","sourceText":"2 hard-boiled egg yolks","amountText":"2 hard-boiled egg yolks","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 tablespoon butter","sourceText":"1 tablespoon butter","amountText":"1 tablespoon butter","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"Oyster juice/liquor (optional)","sourceText":"Oyster juice/liquor (optional)","amountText":"Oyster juice/liquor (optional)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"Ground cayenne pepper","sourceText":"Ground cayenne pepper","amountText":"Ground cayenne pepper","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"Ground mace","sourceText":"Ground mace","amountText":"Ground mace","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","n